# Docker build context (repo root). Keeps the image build small and ensures
# no secrets or host-built artifacts (node_modules/.next/out, local DBs) are
# sent to the Docker daemon.
# NOTE: .git is intentionally NOT excluded — local builds from a full
# checkout ship repo history so Codebase Lab's repo="self" works; the
# Dockerfile copies it only when present (Render's context has no .git).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.venv/

# Node / Next.js (built inside the image, stage 1)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/

# Data & logs (only data/synthetic_history.csv is copied by the Dockerfile)
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
data/*.sqlite*
data/demo_repos/
*.log

# Local planning docs (in-repo copies live in docs/)
/checklist.md
/info.md
/spec.md
